            "question": "What are three different parts of a web page that a browser handles separately when it renders the page?",
            "weakness_tag": "focus_completeness",
            "transcript": "The different parts of a web page that a browser handles handles separately when it renders the page is one, the HTML parsing. This is the one that browse the HTML code to create a document object object model. Number two is DCSS parsing. This browser process CSS files to create the CSS object. And the number three is the rendering. The browser combines the DOM and the CSS OM to create a render tree.",
